    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "cycle-and-turnaround-engine",
      "narrative": "G7 anchors the seventh-sounds section. Ch.2 p.15: 'The first three chords illustrate movement around G7. The next four chords illustrate a substitute turn-around back to G13, followed by a cycle seventh movement.' Dominant sevenths drive both the local turnaround and the extended cycle.",
