    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "sustain-common-tone-across-chord-change",
      "narrative": "Pass instructs sustaining the lead note from one dominant voicing to the next. Ch.2 p.24: 'NOTE: Try to sustain lead notes from one chord to the next. For example, C9 to F13, sustain the G on top.' The common G is held across the II\u2013V motion rather than re-attacked.",
