    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "ii-chord-with-chromatic-approach-to-dominant",
      "narrative": "Dm7 initiates the minor-seventh-to-seventh passage and resolves via a chromatic intermediate. Ch.2 p.15: 'First four chords illustrate movement in Dm7, resolving into Ab13 to G13.' The chromatic Ab13 is inserted as an approach dominant between the ii-chord and the diatonic V13.",
