    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7b9",
      "function_role": "v7b9-in-half-dim-dominant-cadence",
      "narrative": "A7b9 precedes Dm7b5 in the ii\u00f8\u2013V7b9 passage. Ch.2 p.15: 'A7b9 to Dm7b5 resolving finally to G aug.' The b9 dominant is the V chord in a minor-key ii\u00f8\u2013V pairing, with the cadence landing on an augmented rather than a tonic minor chord.",
